{
  "_readme": [
    "Mock benchmark fixtures (P1-12). Each fixture scripts a panel with fake providers; tests/benchmark/test_invariants.py runs every fixture through the real orchestrator and checks the invariants that must hold for it.",
    "A delegate: name; say (a word stem that makes its answer unique, 30 words long); copy_of (reuse another delegate's exact answer); dissent (a marker sentence appended); conclusion and confidence (closing lines appended); same_as (use that delegate's configured provider identity); base, model, alias, family (provider identity); reports (the model the provider reports); fail: error | empty | blank | timeout.",
    "critic: true (answers), false (none configured), fail (primary fails, no fallback), fallback (primary fails, the fallback answers). arbiter: structured | malformed | insufficient | unknown_citation | fallback (primary fails, the fallback answers) | fail.",
    "expect: sources, successes, quorum (met | unmet | single_source_override), judges (do the Critic and Arbiter run), critic_calls and arbiter_calls (provider calls to any Critic or Arbiter provider), single (a single-source run), merged (groups of delegates that must count as one source), reasons (reason per merged group), families, insufficient, format_ok (the Arbiter's structure, null when no Arbiter answered), disclosed (the 'k of n' sentence to find in both judge prompts), max_arbiter_chars."
  ],
